This section is a database adapter that serializes spatial objects into SQL literals. The changed code branches on `is_geometry` and, for rasters, builds a quoted string via `"'%s'::raster" % self.ewkb`. The `self.ewkb` value comes from `to_pgraster`, which produces a hex-encoded string (via `binascii.hexlify(...).upper()` and `pack` of fixed numeric header fields) — not user-controlled free text. This is a serialization/escaping concern (SQL injection class), not an authorization concern (CWE-639/862/863). There is no user-controlled object identifier, no missing/incorrect role or ownership check, and the retrieved policy excerpts concern authentication backends and generic SQL-injection guidance, none of which establish an authorization rule violated by this adapter. No authorization flaw is present in this section.

